Feature: EN 1994 check outcome of committed documents
  A committed before- or after-snapshot of the mutation fixtures is evaluated by the production report and by an independent stress-block formulation of `../../🔮️oracles/🚦️check-outcome/🐍️.py` (composite plastic resistance, shear connection, shear and deflection of the composite beams; continuous end, interior and cantilever spans with PyNite statics and the hogging resistance; composite columns by plastic strip integration of the N-M polygon; composite slabs with partial connection, m-k and vertical shear). The documents `shared://📄️oracle-documents/*` are hand-chosen variants of the span-m after-snapshot, generated by `🧰️scripts/en1994-oracle-documents.py` of the ticket.
  Each row names one check id (a family id reports the worst row of every combination), its status (pass at a utilisation of at most 1, fail above 1) and its utilisation; rows were picked away from the near-limit band so the status is unambiguous.

